  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY NIGHT THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 1155 AM CST Tue Nov 10 2026\n\nA secondary upper level trough and cold front will move south\nthrough the region Wednesday night into Thursday. A cooler air\nmass will advect into the region before the front late this \nweek. Highs on Thursday will range from the upper 40s across \ncentral Missouri to the upper 50s across the far southwestern \nportions of the area. Lows Thursday night into Friday morning \nare expected to drop into the upper 20s to the lower 30s. Highs \non Friday will warm into the middle 40s to around 50 as lows \nFriday night into Saturday morning drop into the lower 20s to \naround 30 degrees. The coldest temperatures will occur across \nthe eastern Ozarks. \n\nHighs will warm into the 50s to near 60s this weekend as an\nupper level ridge moves over the region. The ensemble model\nmembers then show an upper level trough moving southeast across\nthe plains and moving to the south of the area late this weekend\ninto early next week. Moisture return will be limited ahead of\nthis system and the better lift will be to the west of the \narea, but there will be a low, 20-30% chance for a few \nscattered showers mainly west of Highway 65 with this system. \nSome of the model members keep the rainfall associated with this\nsystem west and south the area, so there is the potential much \nof the area remains dry. Highs in the 50s to near 60 are \nexpected to continue into early next week.",
